#ASSERT `Dieu 43: the object of insurance of a property or damage contract` `a property insurance contract` EQUALS `property as the Civil Code defines it`
#ASSERT `Dieu 43: the object of insurance of a property or damage contract` `a damage insurance contract` EQUALS `an economic interest or an obligation under a contract or by law that the insured person bears on a loss`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 43: the object of insurance of a property or damage contract` `a life insurance contract`
`an owner` MEANS `A property or damage contract and a loss` WITH
    `sum insured` IS 0
    `market value of the property at the time of making` IS 0
    `market value of the property at the time and place of the loss` IS 0
    `actual loss` IS 0
    `premium paid` IS 0
    `reasonable costs the contract allows to be deducted` IS 0
    `the policyholder is owner, holds another right in the property or possesses or uses it without owning` IS TRUE
    `the policyholder has a financial interest, financial obligation or liability, or economic loss in respect of the object` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder or insured person has the insurable interest at the time of the loss` IS FALSE
    `the contract agrees otherwise on compensation` IS FALSE
    `the over-insurance was made deliberately` IS FALSE
    `the over-insurance was made through the policyholder's unintentional fault` IS FALSE
    `the insured event has occurred` IS FALSE
    `the loss is natural wear and tear or the inherent nature of the property` IS FALSE
    `costs reasonably and necessarily incurred to prevent and limit the loss` IS 0
    `costs the policyholder or insured person incurred in following the insurer's instructions` IS 0
`a policyholder with a financial interest` MEANS `A property or damage contract and a loss` WITH
    `sum insured` IS 0
    `market value of the property at the time of making` IS 0
    `market value of the property at the time and place of the loss` IS 0
    `actual loss` IS 0
    `premium paid` IS 0
    `reasonable costs the contract allows to be deducted` IS 0
    `the policyholder is owner, holds another right in the property or possesses or uses it without owning` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder has a financial interest, financial obligation or liability, or economic loss in respect of the object` IS TRUE
    `the policyholder or insured person has the insurable interest at the time of the loss` IS FALSE
    `the contract agrees otherwise on compensation` IS FALSE
    `the over-insurance was made deliberately` IS FALSE
    `the over-insurance was made through the policyholder's unintentional fault` IS FALSE
    `the insured event has occurred` IS FALSE
    `the loss is natural wear and tear or the inherent nature of the property` IS FALSE
    `costs reasonably and necessarily incurred to prevent and limit the loss` IS 0
    `costs the policyholder or insured person incurred in following the insurer's instructions` IS 0
`a stranger` MEANS `A property or damage contract and a loss` WITH
    `sum insured` IS 0
    `market value of the property at the time of making` IS 0
    `market value of the property at the time and place of the loss` IS 0
    `actual loss` IS 0
    `premium paid` IS 0
    `reasonable costs the contract allows to be deducted` IS 0
    `the policyholder is owner, holds another right in the property or possesses or uses it without owning` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder has a financial interest, financial obligation or liability, or economic loss in respect of the object` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder or insured person has the insurable interest at the time of the loss` IS FALSE
    `the contract agrees otherwise on compensation` IS FALSE
    `the over-insurance was made deliberately` IS FALSE
    `the over-insurance was made through the policyholder's unintentional fault` IS FALSE
    `the insured event has occurred` IS FALSE
    `the loss is natural wear and tear or the inherent nature of the property` IS FALSE
    `costs reasonably and necessarily incurred to prevent and limit the loss` IS 0
    `costs the policyholder or insured person incurred in following the insurer's instructions` IS 0
`a policyholder with interest at the loss` MEANS `A property or damage contract and a loss` WITH
    `sum insured` IS 0
    `market value of the property at the time of making` IS 0
    `market value of the property at the time and place of the loss` IS 0
    `actual loss` IS 0
    `premium paid` IS 0
    `reasonable costs the contract allows to be deducted` IS 0
    `the policyholder is owner, holds another right in the property or possesses or uses it without owning` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder has a financial interest, financial obligation or liability, or economic loss in respect of the object` IS FALSE
    `the policyholder or insured person has the insurable interest at the time of the loss` IS TRUE
    `the contract agrees otherwise on compensation` IS FALSE
    `the over-insurance was made deliberately` IS FALSE
    `the over-insurance was made through the policyholder's unintentional fault` IS FALSE
    `the insured event has occurred` IS FALSE
    `the loss is natural wear and tear or the inherent nature of the property` IS FALSE
    `costs reasonably and necessarily incurred to prevent and limit the loss` IS 0
    `costs the policyholder or insured person incurred in following the insurer's instructions` IS 0
#ASSERT `Dieu 44(1): the policyholder has an insurable interest in the insured property` `an owner`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 44(1): the policyholder has an insurable interest in the insured property` `a stranger`
#ASSERT `Dieu 44(2): the policyholder has an insurable interest in the damage` `a policyholder with a financial interest`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 44(2): the policyholder has an insurable interest in the damage` `a stranger`
#ASSERT `Dieu 44(3): the insurable interest exists at the time of the loss` `a policyholder with interest at the loss`
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 44(3): the insurable interest exists at the time of the loss` `an owner`

